/* =====================================================================
   Refractory / Unexplained Chronic Cough (RCC) — QSP Mechanistic Map
   Cough Hypersensitivity Syndrome
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE ORGANISING IDEA

     CHRONIC COUGH IS NOT A SYMPTOM OF SOMETHING ELSE.
     IT IS A DISORDER OF THE COUGH REFLEX ARC ITSELF.

   For fifty years chronic cough was managed as a search for a cause —
   asthma, reflux, post-nasal drip — and treated by treating the cause.
   That paradigm fails in roughly 20-40% of specialist-clinic patients,
   and it fails in a specific and informative way: the "causes" get
   treated, the objective evidence of them disappears, and the cough
   does not. Inhaled corticosteroids do nothing without eosinophils.
   Proton-pump inhibitors do nothing without acid. Both are on this map
   precisely so that the model can reproduce their FAILURE.

   The modern reframing (Chung, Morice, McGarvey, Mazzone, Undem) is
   that refractory chronic cough is a NEUROPATHIC disorder of the vagal
   reflex arc, the airway analogue of neuropathic pain, with the same
   two hallmark abnormalities:

       HYPERTUSSIA  exaggerated cough to a tussive stimulus  (hyperalgesia)
       ALLOTUSSIA   cough to a stimulus that should not evoke it, e.g.
                    talking, laughing, cold air, aerosol, perfume   (allodynia)

   plus LARYNGEAL PARAESTHESIA — the "tickle" — which is the airway
   equivalent of spontaneous neuropathic pain and which, crucially,
   arises from ECTOPIC AFFERENT DISCHARGE, i.e. from the nerve itself
   rather than from anything in the airway. A patient can cough with a
   completely normal airway.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE THREE LAYERS, AND WHY THE MAP IS DRAWN THIS WAY

     LAYER 1  PERIPHERAL GAIN  (what the airway does to the nerve)
              epithelial damage -> pannexin-1 -> extracellular ATP
              -> P2X3 homotrimers on vagal C-fibre terminals; plus
              NGF/TrkA, PGE2/EP3, bradykinin/B2 and acid/ASIC
              sensitising TRPV1 and TRPA1 and up-regulating P2X3 itself.
              This is the layer every P2X3 antagonist acts on.

     LAYER 2  CENTRAL GAIN  (what the nerve does to the brainstem)
              sustained afferent barrage -> nTS second-order neuron
              NMDA-dependent WIND-UP, substance P/NK-1, loss of
              GABA/glycinergic inhibition, microglial BDNF. This is the
              layer that makes the disorder OUTLIVE ITS TRIGGER, and it
              is the layer gabapentin, pregabalin, morphine and
              amitriptyline act on.

     LAYER 3  CORTICAL CONTROL  (what the person does about it)
              Cough is unique among airway reflexes in being under
              conscious control. Afferent drive first becomes the
              conscious URGE TO COUGH (insula/ACC), and only then, if
              descending prefrontal suppression is insufficient, a
              motor cough. This layer is why speech-and-language
              therapy works, why cough is near-abolished during sleep,
              and — the single most important fact for anyone designing
              a cough trial — why the PLACEBO RESPONSE IN OBJECTIVE
              COUGH COUNTS IS ~30%.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE VICIOUS CIRCLE (bold red edges on the map)

     afferent barrage -> nTS wind-up -> central gain -> more cough
     -> laryngeal mechanical trauma -> epithelial damage -> ATP
     -> afferent barrage

   Above a critical loop gain this circle is SELF-SUSTAINING: remove the
   original insult and the cough persists. Below it, the same insult
   produces a post-viral cough that resolves in 8 weeks. In the
   accompanying mrgsolve model the disease is GENERATED by this
   bistability rather than assumed — a single insult amplitude decides
   whether the virtual patient recovers or becomes refractory.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE CENTRAL PHARMACOLOGICAL CLAIM OF THIS MAP

   Four P2X3 antagonists have been taken into phase 2b/3 chronic cough
   trials. They share ONE efficacy mechanism and differ in ONE number —
   selectivity for the homotrimeric P2X3 receptor on vagal afferents
   over the heterotrimeric P2X2/3 receptor on type II/III taste cells:

     gefapixant   selectivity ~1x     efficacy YES (modest)  taste AE 58-69%
     eliapixant   selectivity ~60x    efficacy YES (modest)  taste AE ~10-20%
                                      TERMINATED for idiosyncratic DILI
     sivopixant   selectivity ~30x    efficacy NOT confirmed taste AE ~6-13%
     camlipixant  selectivity ~1500x  efficacy YES (larger)  taste AE ~6-10%

   Efficacy and dysgeusia are therefore NOT independent for gefapixant —
   they are two readouts of the same occupancy curve, separated only by
   the selectivity ratio. The map draws them as a single drug node
   projecting to two receptor nodes, and the model reproduces all four
   compounds by changing that one parameter.

   And because the P2X3 pathway carries only part of the tussive drive,
   the class has a CEILING: complete target coverage still leaves the
   TRPV1/TRPA1/mechanical arm intact. That is why no P2X3 antagonist has
   ever produced the near-abolition of cough that morphine can.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE DIAGNOSTIC DISSOCIATION THE MAP PREDICTS

   P2X3 antagonists strongly suppress ATP-evoked cough and barely shift
   the capsaicin C5 threshold, because capsaicin bypasses P2X3 entirely
   and gates TRPV1 directly. Both challenge outputs are drawn, and both
   are computed in the model, so this is a prediction rather than an
   assertion.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Legend
     ellipse / box        biological species, state or process
     hexagon              drug or intervention
     octagon              clinical endpoint or patient-reported outcome
     diamond              measurement / challenge test
     doubleoctagon        on-target adverse effect
     solid arrow          activation / increase
     T-bar (tee)          inhibition / decrease
     dashed               slow, transcriptional or plastic change
     bold red             the self-sustaining vicious circle
     blue                 pharmacological intervention
     orange               adverse effect / tolerability limit
   ===================================================================== */

digraph RCC_QSP {
  graph [rankdir=TB, newrank=true, splines=spline, overlap=false, nodesep=0.22,
         ranksep=0.62, fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=11,
         labelloc="t", compound=true, bgcolor="white",
         label=<<b>Refractory Chronic Cough — Cough Hypersensitivity Syndrome</b><br/>
                <font point-size="12">QSP mechanistic map · peripheral gain → central gain → cortical control · P2X3 efficacy/dysgeusia selectivity window</font>>];
  node  [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9, style="filled", penwidth=0.9];
  edge  [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=8, arrowsize=0.6, penwidth=0.9, color="#555555"];

  /* ================================================================
     1. TRIGGERS AND UPSTREAM EXPOSURES
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_trig {
    label="1 · 유발 인자 및 노출 (Triggers & Exposures)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#B0BEC5"; fillcolor="#ECEFF1"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#CFD8DC", color="#78909C"];

    T_VIRUS   [label="호흡기 바이러스 감염\nRespiratory viral infection\n(rhinovirus, RSV, influenza,\nSARS-CoV-2)"];
    T_POSTVIR [label="감염 후 기침\nPost-infectious cough\n(≈50% of new-onset RCC\ndates to an infection)"];
    T_ACEI    [label="ACE 억제제\nACE inhibitor\n(5-20% incidence, F>M)"];
    T_SMOKE   [label="흡연 / 대기오염\nTobacco smoke, PM2.5,\nozone, occupational irritants"];
    T_ALLERG  [label="흡입 알레르겐\nInhaled allergen\n(Th2 sensitisation)"];
    T_REFLUX  [label="위식도 역류 (산성/비산성)\nGastro-oesophageal reflux\nacid + non-acid + gaseous"];
    T_UACS    [label="상기도 기침 증후군\nUpper airway cough syndrome\n(rhinosinusitis, post-nasal drip)"];
    T_IPF     [label="폐 실질 견인\nParenchymal distortion\n(IPF, bronchiectasis)"];
    T_SURG    [label="수술/삽관 후 후두 손상\nPost-intubation or\npost-surgical laryngeal injury"];
    T_MENO    [label="폐경 이행\nMenopausal transition\n(oestrogen withdrawal;\nTRPV1 modulation)"];
    T_GENE    [label="유전적 소인\nGenetic predisposition\n(TRPV1 I585V, family history\nof chronic cough)"];
    T_AGE     [label="연령 / 성별\nAge 55-65, female 2:1\n(lower capsaicin C5\nin women, 2-4x)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     2. AIRWAY EPITHELIUM AND ATP RELEASE
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_epi {
    label="2 · 기도 상피 손상과 ATP 유리 (Airway Epithelium & ATP Release)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#8D6E63"; fillcolor="#EFEBE9"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#D7CCC8", color="#8D6E63"];

    EPI_INT  [label="상피 완전성\nEpithelial integrity\n(tight junctions, ZO-1,\nE-cadherin)"];
    EPI_DAM  [label="상피 손상/탈락\nEpithelial damage\n& desquamation"];
    PANX1    [label="Pannexin-1 hemichannel\n(mechanical + inflammatory\ngating)"];
    ATP_REL  [label="세포외 ATP 유리\nExtracellular ATP release\n(airway surface liquid)"];
    ATP_ASL  [label="기도표면 ATP 농도\n[ATP] in ASL\n(RCC sputum ATP ↑↑)"];
    ENTPD    [label="CD39 / CD73 ectonucleotidase\nATP → ADP → AMP → adenosine"];
    ADENO    [label="아데노신\nAdenosine\n(A1/A2A on afferents)"];
    MUCUS    [label="점액 과분비\nMucus hypersecretion\nMUC5AC / MUC5B"];
    MCC      [label="점액섬모 청소율\nMucociliary clearance"];
    MECHSTR  [label="기계적 전단 응력\nMechanical shear stress\nfrom coughing itself"];
    OSMO     [label="삼투압 스트레스\nOsmotic / hypertonic stress\n(mannitol, distilled water)"];
    EPI_REP  [label="상피 재생\nEpithelial repair\n(EGFR, slow: weeks)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     3. AIRWAY INFLAMMATION AND IMMUNE CELLS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_infl {
    label="3 · 기도 염증 (Airway Inflammation — the treatable-trait layer)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#EF9A9A"; fillcolor="#FFEBEE"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#FFCDD2", color="#E57373"];

    TH2      [label="Th2 / ILC2\nIL-4, IL-5, IL-13"];
    EOS      [label="호산구\nAirway eosinophils\n(NAEB, cough-variant asthma)"];
    EOSPROD  [label="호산구 과립단백\nECP, MBP, EPO,\neosinophil peroxidase"];
    MAST     [label="비만세포\nMast cells\n(airway smooth muscle\ninfiltration)"];
    HIST     [label="히스타민\nHistamine → H1"];
    PGD2     [label="PGD2 → DP2 / CRTH2"];
    TRYPT    [label="트립타제\nTryptase → PAR-2"];
    NEUT     [label="호중구\nNeutrophils, IL-8,\nneutrophil elastase"];
    MACRO    [label="폐포 대식세포\nAlveolar macrophages"];
    NFKB     [label="NF-κB / MAPK\nairway inflammatory\ntranscription"];
    IL33     [label="알라민\nAlarmins: IL-33, TSLP,\nIL-25"];
    FENO     [label="FeNO\n(호기 산화질소)"];
    COX2     [label="COX-2 유도\nCOX-2 induction"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     4. REFLUX AND LARYNGOPHARYNGEAL AXIS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_refl {
    label="4 · 역류 및 후두인두 축 (Reflux & Laryngopharyngeal Axis)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#A5D6A7"; fillcolor="#E8F5E9"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#C8E6C9", color="#66BB6A"];

    LES      [label="하부식도 괄약근 압력\nLower oesophageal\nsphincter pressure"];
    TLESR    [label="일과성 LES 이완\nTransient LES relaxations\n(vagally mediated)"];
    ACIDREF  [label="산 역류\nAcid reflux\npH < 4 events"];
    NONACID  [label="비산성/약산성 역류\nNon-acid & weakly acidic\nreflux, gaseous reflux"];
    PEPSIN   [label="펩신 / 담즙산\nPepsin & bile acids\n(laryngeal mucosal injury)"];
    ASPIRA   [label="미세 흡인\nMicro-aspiration"];
    OESVAGAL [label="식도-기관지 미주신경 반사\nOesophago-bronchial\nvagal reflex"];
    LPR      [label="후두인두 역류 소견\nLaryngopharyngeal reflux signs\n(RSI, RFS scores)"];
    COUGHREF [label="기침→복압 상승→역류\nCough → intra-abdominal\npressure → more reflux"];
    HIATUS   [label="열공 헤르니아\nHiatus hernia,\ndelayed gastric emptying"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     5. SENSITISING MEDIATORS AND NEUROTROPHINS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_med {
    label="5 · 감작 매개물질 및 신경영양인자 (Sensitising Mediators & Neurotrophins)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#FFB74D"; fillcolor="#FFF3E0"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#FFE0B2", color="#FB8C00"];

    NGF      [label="신경성장인자\nNGF → TrkA / p75\n(↑ in RCC airway)"];
    BDNF_P   [label="BDNF (peripheral)\nartemin, GDNF"];
    PGE2     [label="PGE2 → EP3 receptor\n(the classic tussive\nprostanoid)"];
    BK       [label="브래디키닌\nBradykinin → B2 receptor"];
    SUBP_P   [label="Substance P / CGRP / NKA\n(peripheral release,\nneurogenic inflammation)"];
    PROTON   [label="H+ / 산성화\nLuminal acidification\n→ ASIC3, TRPV1"];
    LTD4     [label="시스테이닐 류코트리엔\nCysLT → CysLT1"];
    ATPADO   [label="퓨린 신호\nPurinergic signalling\nATP, UTP, adenosine"];
    IL6L     [label="IL-6 / IL-1β (local)\nneuro-immune crosstalk"];
    OXSTR    [label="산화 스트레스\nOxidative stress, ROS,\n4-HNE (TRPA1 agonist)"];
    ESTRO    [label="에스트로겐 / 프로게스테론\nSex steroids modulate\nTRPV1 & NGF"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     6. ION CHANNELS AND RECEPTORS ON VAGAL AFFERENT TERMINALS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_chan {
    label="6 · 미주신경 종말 이온채널 및 수용체 (Afferent Terminal Ion Channels & Receptors)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#7986CB"; fillcolor="#E8EAF6"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, style="filled,rounded", fillcolor="#C5CAE9", color="#5C6BC0"];

    P2X3     [label="P2X3 동종삼량체\nP2X3 homotrimer\n(jugular/nodose C-fibre)\nATP-gated cation channel"];
    P2X23    [label="P2X2/3 이종삼량체\nP2X2/3 heterotrimer\n(slowly desensitising)"];
    P2X3EXP  [label="P2X3 발현 상향조절\nP2X3 up-regulation\n(NGF-driven, DAYS-WEEKS)"];
    TRPV1    [label="TRPV1\ncapsaicin, H+, heat,\nanandamide, 12-HPETE"];
    TRPA1    [label="TRPA1\nacrolein, cinnamaldehyde,\n4-HNE, cold"];
    TRPM8    [label="TRPM8\ncold, menthol\n(ANTI-tussive when activated)"];
    ASIC3    [label="ASIC3\nacid-sensing ion channel"];
    NAV17    [label="Nav1.7 / Nav1.8 / Nav1.9\naction potential initiation\nand conduction"];
    KV       [label="Kv7 / KCa channels\nmembrane stabilisation\n(brake on excitability)"];
    NK1P     [label="NK-1 / NK-2 (peripheral)"];
    B2R      [label="B2 bradykinin receptor"];
    EP3R     [label="EP3 prostanoid receptor"];
    A2CH     [label="α2δ-1 subunit\n(Ca_v accessory, up-regulated\nin neuropathic states)"];
    MOR_P    [label="μ-opioid receptor\n(peripheral terminals)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     7. VAGAL AFFERENT SUBTYPES
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_aff {
    label="7 · 미주신경 구심성 섬유 아형 (Vagal Afferent Subtypes)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#4DB6AC"; fillcolor="#E0F2F1"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#B2DFDB", color="#26A69A"];

    JUG_C    [label="Jugular C-fibre\n(neural-crest derived)\nTRPV1+, P2X3+, TAC1+\n→ URGE + cough"];
    NOD_C    [label="Nodose C-fibre\n(placode derived)\nP2X2/3+, 5-HT3+"];
    AD_COUGH [label="Nodose Aδ 'cough receptor'\nlow-threshold mechanosensor,\nacid-sensitive, P2X3+\n→ the classic cough afferent"];
    RAR      [label="RAR / SAR\nrapidly & slowly adapting\nstretch receptors"];
    SLN      [label="상후두신경 (SLN)\nSuperior laryngeal nerve\nlaryngeal mucosal afferents"];
    EXTRAP   [label="기도외 구심성\nExtrapulmonary afferents\nnasal, pharyngeal, oesophageal,\nauricular (Arnold's) branch"];
    AFIRE    [label="통합 구심성 발화율\nIntegrated afferent\nfiring rate (Hz)"];
    ECTOPIC  [label="이소성 자발 발화\nECTOPIC spontaneous discharge\n→ laryngeal paraesthesia,\nthe 'tickle' with a normal airway"];
    PERIPHSENS [label="말초 감작 상태\nPERIPHERAL SENSITISATION\nlowered activation threshold,\nrecruitment of silent afferents"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     8. BRAINSTEM: nTS SECOND-ORDER PROCESSING
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_nts {
    label="8 · 뇌간 고립로핵 처리 (Brainstem nTS Second-Order Processing)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#BA68C8"; fillcolor="#F3E5F5"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#E1BEE7", color="#AB47BC"];

    NTS      [label="고립로핵 (nTS)\nNucleus tractus solitarius\n2nd-order relay neurons"];
    NMDA     [label="NMDA 수용체\nNMDA-R (GluN2B)\nMg2+ block relief"];
    AMPA     [label="AMPA / kainate\nfast glutamatergic\ntransmission"];
    SUBP_C   [label="Substance P → NK-1\n(central terminals)\nslow depolarisation"];
    GABAI    [label="GABA_A / 글리신 억제성 개재뉴런\nGABAergic & glycinergic\ninterneurons (the brake)"];
    MICROG   [label="미세아교세포 활성화\nMicroglial activation\np38 MAPK, BDNF release"];
    ASTRO    [label="성상교세포\nAstrocyte glutamate\nre-uptake (GLT-1)"];
    WINDUP   [label="Wind-up / 중추 감작\nCENTRAL SENSITISATION\nuse-dependent amplification\nof synaptic gain"];
    PSNEUR   [label="Paratrigeminal nucleus (Pa5)\njugular C-fibre relay\n→ urge/affective route"];
    CVLM     [label="Caudal VLM / RVLM\nrespiratory pattern\nintegration"];
    SEROT    [label="5-HT3 / 5-HT2A\nserotonergic modulation"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     9. DESCENDING MODULATION
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_desc {
    label="9 · 하행 조절 (Descending Modulation — the endogenous brake)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#9575CD"; fillcolor="#EDE7F6"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#D1C4E9", color="#7E57C2"];

    PAG      [label="수도관 주위 회백질 (PAG)\nPeriaqueductal grey"];
    RVM      [label="Rostral ventromedial medulla\nON-cells (facilitation) /\nOFF-cells (inhibition)"];
    RAPHE    [label="Raphe / 세로토닌계\nSerotonergic descending"];
    LC       [label="청반 (LC)\nLocus coeruleus\nnoradrenergic → α2"];
    ENKEPH   [label="내인성 오피오이드\nEnkephalin / β-endorphin\n→ μ, δ, κ receptors"];
    DESCINH  [label="하행 억제 긴장도\nDESCENDING INHIBITORY TONE\n(reduced in RCC and by\nsleep deprivation)"];
    DESCFAC  [label="하행 촉진\nDescending facilitation\n(anxiety, catastrophising,\nhypervigilance)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     10. CORTICAL NETWORK AND URGE TO COUGH
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_cort {
    label="10 · 피질 네트워크와 기침 충동 (Cortical Network & Urge to Cough)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#4FC3F7"; fillcolor="#E1F5FE"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#B3E5FC", color="#29B6F6"];

    THAL     [label="시상 (VPM)\nThalamic relay"];
    INSULA   [label="섬엽 (insula)\nprimary interoceptive\nrepresentation of airway"];
    ACC      [label="전대상피질 (ACC)\naffective salience,\nunpleasantness of the urge"];
    S1       [label="일차 감각피질 (S1/S2)\nlocalisation of the\nlaryngeal 'tickle'"];
    URGE     [label="기침 충동 (Uc)\nURGE TO COUGH\nconscious premonitory\nsensation — LOWER threshold\nthan the motor cough"];
    PFC      [label="배외측 전전두엽 (dlPFC)\nvoluntary suppression\nnetwork"];
    CORTSUP  [label="피질 억제 용량\nCORTICAL SUPPRESSION CAPACITY\n— the substrate of SLT and\nof the placebo response"];
    HYPERVIG [label="과각성/파국화\nHypervigilance,\ncough catastrophising scale\n(anxiety, depression)"];
    HABIT    [label="학습된 기침 행동\nLearned / habitual cough\nbehaviour, operant\nreinforcement"];
    ATTEN    [label="주의 배분\nAttentional load\n(distraction reduces cough)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     11. COUGH MOTOR PATTERN GENERATOR AND EFFERENTS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_motor {
    label="11 · 기침 운동 패턴 생성기 (Cough Motor Pattern Generator & Efferents)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#FFD54F"; fillcolor="#FFFDE7"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#FFF9C4", color="#FBC02D"];

    CPG      [label="기침 패턴 생성기\nCough pattern generator\n(medullary respiratory\nnetwork reconfiguration)"];
    THRESH   [label="기침 역치\nCOUGH THRESHOLD\n(drive must exceed this)"];
    INSP     [label="흡기상\nInspiratory phase\n(phrenic, external\nintercostals)"];
    COMPR    [label="압축상\nCompressive phase\nglottic closure\n(recurrent laryngeal n.)"];
    EXPUL    [label="배출상\nExpulsive phase\nabdominal + internal\nintercostal, glottal opening"];
    BOUT     [label="기침 발작 구조\nCough bout structure\n(epochs, bursts,\ncoughs per bout)"];
    LARYSPAS [label="후두 경련/역설적 성대운동\nLaryngospasm & paradoxical\nvocal fold movement"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     12. CIRCADIAN AND SLEEP GATING
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_circ {
    label="12 · 일주기 및 수면 게이팅 (Circadian & Sleep Gating)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#90A4AE"; fillcolor="#ECEFF1"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#CFD8DC", color="#78909C"];

    CIRCOSC  [label="일주기 진동자\nCircadian oscillator\n(SCN, cortisol rhythm)"];
    AWAKE    [label="각성 상태 게이트\nAWAKE / ASLEEP gate"];
    SLEEPSUP [label="수면 중 기침 억제\nCough is near-ABOLISHED in\nsleep: cortical urge pathway\nis offline"];
    MORNPEAK [label="아침 기상 후 정점\nMorning post-waking peak\n(overnight secretion load\n+ reflex re-engagement)"];
    SLEEPFRAG [label="수면 분절\nSleep fragmentation,\ninsomnia, fatigue"];
    SLEEPDEB [label="수면 부채 → 하행 억제 저하\nSleep debt degrades\ndescending inhibition"];
    AWAKEF   [label="각성 시 기침 빈도\nAWAKE cough frequency\n(≈1.5x the 24-h rate)"];
  }

